---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Kane County Surveillance | NoRec.US"
  description="Documented Kane County surveillance systems, including Kane County Sheriff Flock ALPR, Getac body and in-car video, Evidence.com eDiscovery, and municipal drone programs."
  active="surveillance"
>
<main class="page_shell">
  <header class="article_header">
    <p class="eyebrow">LOCAL SURVEILLANCE · KANE COUNTY, ILLINOIS</p>
    <h1>Kane County</h1>
    <p class="article_deck">County records document a Sheriff's Office Flock network, body and in-car video systems, cloud evidence management, and additional municipal drone programs.</p>
  </header>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">KANE COUNTY SHERIFF'S OFFICE · ALPR</p>
    <h2>25 Flock readers documented in the 2025 renewal</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>25 Flock cameras</h3>
        <p>A 2025 Kane County resolution states the Sheriff's Office was renewing Flock Safety service for 25 license-plate reader cameras dispersed countywide.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>$61,000 renewal</h3>
        <p>The renewal authorized $61,000 for calendar year 2025.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Government complexes included</h3>
        <p>The resolution specifically identifies readers at the Judicial Center complex and Government Center among the countywide deployment.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">UNKNOWN</span>
        <h3>Current 2026 configuration</h3>
        <p>The 2025 renewal establishes the documented count for that contract year. The published source set does not establish a 2026 renewal, current inventory, retention configuration, sharing list, or audit results.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
    <details class="surveillance_sources" open>
      <summary>Source</summary>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="https://www.kanecountyil.gov/Lists/Events/Attachments/7382/AG%20PKT%2025-01%20JPS.pdf">Kane County — 2025 Flock Safety renewal packet</a></li>
      </ul>
    </details>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">BODY / IN-CAR VIDEO</p>
    <h2>Getac system approved for the Sheriff's Office</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Five-year Getac lease</h3>
        <p>A 2020 Kane County resolution authorized a five-year lease through Midwest Public Safety Group for a Getac in-car and body-worn camera system.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Front, rear, and prisoner-compartment video</h3>
        <p>The county's executive summary describes front, back-seat, and rear camera capture together with body-worn video.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Cloud-hosted evidence management</h3>
        <p>The same record describes browser-based cloud review, retention-rule tagging, restrictive access controls, and an evidence-management back end for video, pictures, and documents.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">COUNTY EDISCOVERY</p>
    <h2>Evidence.com adopted by the State's Attorney's Office</h2>
    <p>Kane County Finance Committee minutes from 2022 record the State's Attorney's selection of Axon Evidence.com for eDiscovery. The discussion cites unlimited storage, auto-transcription, keyword search, and compatibility with video evidence from Axon and non-Axon sources.</p>
    <div class="evidence_box">
      <span class="status_label">SCOPE</span>
      <p>This is a Kane County State's Attorney evidence-management relationship, not proof that the Sheriff's body-camera system itself had switched from Getac to Axon.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">MUNICIPAL DRONES</p>
    <h2>State reporting documents UAS programs inside the county</h2>
    <div class="finding_grid">
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>South Elgin Police</h3>
        <p>The SFY 2024 state report lists two drones and 43 flights, including multiple training flights at the Kane County Sheriff's Office.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">DOCUMENTED</span>
        <h3>Batavia Police</h3>
        <p>The same statewide reporting dataset lists Batavia Police as owning one drone.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">SECONDARY-SOURCE CONFIRMED</span>
        <h3>Elgin Police</h3>
        <p>EFF's index of the statewide report lists nine Elgin Police drones and 73 flights during the SFY 2024 reporting period. NoRec therefore treats these figures as secondary-source confirmed rather than as a primary-source finding.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span class="status_label">SECONDARY-SOURCE CONFIRMED</span>
        <h3>North Aurora Police</h3>
        <p>EFF's index of the same report lists four North Aurora Police drones and 12 flights during the reporting period.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">PRIMARY SOURCES</p>
    <ul class="provider_source_list">
      <li><a href="https://www.kanecountyil.gov/Lists/Events/Attachments/7382/AG%20PKT%2025-01%20JPS.pdf">Kane County — 2025 Sheriff's Flock Safety renewal</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.kanecountyil.gov/MeetingMinutes/5452/20-07-14%20COB%20minutes-full.pdf">Kane County — 2020 Getac in-car/body-worn camera lease</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.kanecountyil.gov/MeetingMinutes/6392/22-11-23.pdf">Kane County Finance Committee — Evidence.com eDiscovery discussion</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://agency.icjia-api.cloud/uploads/SFY_24_Drone_Report_with_Appendices_491dfa4810.pdf">Illinois SFY 2024 Freedom from Drone Surveillance Act report</a></li>
      <li><a href="https://www.kanecountyil.gov/Lists/DepartmentsAndOffices/AllItems.aspx">Kane County — FOIA contacts</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <p class="eyebrow">UNRESOLVED</p>
    <h2>Not established by the published records.</h2>
    <ul class="about_questions">
      <li>The current Kane County Sheriff Flock contract, reader inventory and locations, retention, sharing, authorized-user count, and audit results.</li>
      <li>The status of the Sheriff's Getac body/in-car video system after the original five-year lease term.</li>
      <li>The Sheriff's current drone inventory and flight reporting.</li>
      <li>Primary municipal records for ALPR, drones, body cameras, and evidence systems in Aurora, Elgin, Batavia, South Elgin, North Aurora, St. Charles, Geneva, and other Kane County municipalities.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
